{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.SharedDenominatorCuspHolonomy","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.SharedDenominatorCuspHolonomy","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Complex.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QPochhammer.seed_is_not_the_cusp_shape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QPochhammer.seed_is_not_the_cusp_shape","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/shared-denominator-cusp-holonomy.lean#L161-L188","doc":"**The bare algebraic seed is not the cusp shape.**\n\nAt a root index the matched shape is not a real number, so no real seed —\n`q^{-k}` included — equals `shape k`.  The pole-to-cusp correspondence is a\nbijection of *labels*, and the shape parameter is a non-trivial function of\nthe seed.\n\nThe `.md` reaches this empirically: `snappy-cusp-seeding.witness.json`\nmeasures the bare seeds at distance `0.4`–`0.9` from SnapPy's `z_k` for\n`m004`, `m003` and `L6a4`, and concludes the identity `q₀^{-k} = z_k` cannot\nhold.  Here it follows from the conjecture itself, since `im_pos` excludes\nevery real shape.\n\nThis replaces `newton_seed_completeness`, which had the same type as\n`shared_denominator_cusp_holonomy` above and a docstring claiming a\nNewton–Raphson seeding property its statement did not contain. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QPochhammer.shared_denominator_cusp_holonomy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QPochhammer.shared_denominator_cusp_holonomy","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/shared-denominator-cusp-holonomy.lean#L142-L159","doc":"**Shared-denominator cusp holonomy**\n([`conj:shared-denominator-cusp-holonomy`]), in consequence form.\n\nAt an algebraic denominator zero, the matched cusp shape has non-zero\nimaginary part and is neither of the two degenerate shapes.\n\nDerived: the conclusion is a conjunction of three consequences of\n`GeometricShape (shape k)`, not that proposition, so this is not the class\nfield restated.  The previous version *was* — it read\n`:= h.cusp_complete_of_root`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:shared-denominator-cusp-holonomy","label":"conj:shared-denominator-cusp-holonomy","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/shared-denominator-cusp-holonomy.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QPochhammer.SharedDenominatorCuspHolonomy.cusp_complete_of_root","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QPochhammer.SharedDenominatorCuspHolonomy.cusp_complete_of_root","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/shared-denominator-cusp-holonomy.lean#L139-L139","doc":"For each algebraic denominator zero `x = q^{-k}` (i.e. each\n`k < n` with `1 - x q^k = 0`), the matched complex cusp shape\nparameter `shape k` is `GeometricShape`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QPochhammer.SharedDenominatorCuspHolonomy.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QPochhammer.SharedDenominatorCuspHolonomy.mk","kind":"ctor","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/shared-denominator-cusp-holonomy.lean#L133-L133","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QPochhammer.SharedDenominatorCuspHolonomy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QPochhammer.SharedDenominatorCuspHolonomy","kind":"class","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/shared-denominator-cusp-holonomy.lean#L120-L140","doc":"The shared-denominator conjecture, packaged as a typeclass over a\nstate variable `x`, substrate parameter `q`, depth `n`, and the\n**cusp shape assignment** `shape : Fin n → ℂ`.\n\nAn instance asserts that whenever the algebraic denominator `(x; q)_n`\nvanishes at a root of the form `x = q^{-k}`, the *matched* cusp shape\nparameter `shape k` satisfies the Thurston cusp-completeness predicate.\n\n`shape` is a **parameter**, not a field.  That is what makes the class a\nhypothesis about the caller's cusp data rather than about an assignment\nthe instance chose — see `exists_geometricShape` and the module docstring\nfor what happened when the shape was existentially quantified instead. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QPochhammer.exists_geometricShape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QPochhammer.exists_geometricShape","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/shared-denominator-cusp-holonomy.lean#L102-L118","doc":"**A geometric shape exists**, witnessed by `z = i`.\n\nRecorded as a theorem because it is the reason the previous encoding of this\nconjecture was empty.  The old class field concluded `∃ z : ℂ,\nGeometricShape z` with no link to the root index, and that is exactly this\nstatement — so the class was inhabited for every `q`, `x`, `n` by a constant\nwitness, despite the file and the `.md` both asserting it had no instance.\n\n`im_pos` does rule out real constants.  It does not rule out constants. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QPochhammer.GeometricShape.im_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QPochhammer.GeometricShape.im_pos","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/shared-denominator-cusp-holonomy.lean#L100-L100","doc":"Geometric (positively oriented) shape: `Im z > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QPochhammer.GeometricShape.shape_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QPochhammer.GeometricShape.shape_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/shared-denominator-cusp-holonomy.lean#L98-L98","doc":"Shape nondegeneracy: `z ≠ 1` (the degenerate flat vertex; the\nlongitude holonomy equation `Hol_λ(z) = 1` itself remains open). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QPochhammer.GeometricShape.shape_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QPochhammer.GeometricShape.shape_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/shared-denominator-cusp-holonomy.lean#L95-L95","doc":"Shape nondegeneracy: `z ≠ 0` (the degenerate collapsed vertex; the\nmeridian holonomy equation `Hol_μ(z) = 1` itself remains open). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QPochhammer.GeometricShape.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QPochhammer.GeometricShape.mk","kind":"ctor","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/shared-denominator-cusp-holonomy.lean#L92-L92","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QPochhammer.GeometricShape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QPochhammer.GeometricShape","kind":"structure","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/shared-denominator-cusp-holonomy.lean#L80-L100","doc":"The geometric-shape predicate over `ℂ` at the shape parameter `z` —\nthe *necessary* conditions for cusp completeness (the name says what\nit asserts; the full holonomy content remains open, see below):\nthe shape is a **geometric** ideal-tetrahedron shape — non-degenerate\n(`z ≠ 0`, `z ≠ 1`) and of positive imaginary part (upper half-plane,\npositively oriented). A genuine formalisation would additionally carry\nthe ideal triangulation and the Neumann-Zagier potential with\n`Hol_μ(z) = Hol_λ(z) = 1`; those gluing equations remain open here,\nbut `im_pos` already excludes every real (flattened) shape, so the\npredicate is not dischargeable by a *real* constant witness — see\n`exists_geometricShape` for why that is much weaker than it sounds. ","signatureChunk":0}]}